window.STORY={intro:["Your head hurts. Your mouth tastes like copper and cheap ale.","You are lying under a table in a tavern. Someone has tucked a bar rag under your head as a pillow, which was kind.","Your coin purse is gone. Your memory of the last three days is gone with it.","You remember your name. You remember how to fight. You do not remember how you got here.","Somewhere behind the bar, a very large man is polishing a glass and watching you with the patience of someone who has seen this before."],dialogs:{grell:{start:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"Ah. The sleeper wakes. You came in three nights ago with two hooded fellows, drank one cup of my worst ale and went down like a felled oak. They paid for your room and left. You never made it to the room.",choices:[{text:"Hooded fellows? Who were they?",next:"hooded"},{text:"Three nights?! Who took my coin purse?",next:"purse"},{text:"[Intimidation] Tell me everything, barkeep.",check:{skill:"intimidation",dc:12},pass:"intimidated",fail:"intimidateFail"},{text:"Is there work? I'm broke.",next:"work"}]},hooded:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"Didn't catch faces. One had a tattoo on the neck, a spiral like a snail with eyes. Paid in good coin. Too good for this place, frankly.",choices:[{text:"A spiral with eyes…",next:"work",set:{heardSpiral:!0}},{text:"Is there work?",next:"work"}]},purse:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"Not me, and not my regulars, they know better. But I'll tell you what: the rats in my cellar have been dragging off anything shiny for a week. If your purse is anywhere, it's down there. Along with whatever's been eating my cheese.",choices:[{text:"You want me to clear your cellar.",next:"work"}]},intimidated:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:'…Fine. FINE. One of them came back the next morning. Asked if you\'d "said anything strange in your sleep." Slipped me a gold piece to keep quiet. Here, take it, it gives me the creeps. Spiral stamped right on it.',choices:[{text:"Take the coin.",next:"work",action:"giveSigilCoinEarly",set:{heardSpiral:!0}}]},intimidateFail:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"Friend, I have thrown out ogres. Sit down before you fall down. Now: about my cellar…",choices:[{text:"Your cellar?",next:"work"}]},work:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"Rats. Big ones. My cellar's crawling and I've lost a cask of Redwatch brandy to the little fiends. Clear it out, find whatever they've been hoarding, and I'll feed and bed you for a week. The trapdoor's in the corner. Mind the steps. And if you'd rather not go alone, the Guild Hall across the square owes me a favour: your first companion is on the house.",choices:[{text:"I'll do it. (Accept: Something in the Cellar)",action:"acceptQuest:act1",next:"accepted"},{text:"Let me look around first.",next:null}]},accepted:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"Good. Take this torch, it's for the smell. Mostly. And here: twenty gold, on account, for provisions. Quill's sells potions, the smithy sells anything sharp, and if you'd rather not go down alone the Guild Hall is on me. Don't drink it. I'll know.",action:"giveItem:torch;giveGold:20",choices:[{text:"Thanks.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"{gossip}",choices:[{text:"Rest here for the night (long rest).",action:"longRest",next:null},{text:"Buy a round for the room. (5 gp, party morale)",action:"buyRound",next:null},{text:"Just passing through.",next:null}]}},wren:{start:{speaker:"Wren Ashby",text:"You're the one who's been asleep under table four. Don't look so surprised, it's a small tavern. I'm Wren. I find things people lose. For a fee.",choices:[{text:"I lost three days and a purse.",next:"lost"},{text:"[Insight] You already know something about me.",check:{skill:"insight",dc:12},pass:"insight",fail:"insightFail"},{text:"Nice to meet you.",next:null}]},lost:{speaker:"Wren Ashby",text:"Three days is a lot to lose. Purses come back. Days don't. Whoever did this to you used something nasty. Come find me when you have a lead and I'll help you pull the thread.",choices:[{text:"I will.",next:null}]},insight:{speaker:"Wren Ashby",text:"…Sharp. Yes. The men who brought you in weren't just hooded, they were nervous. Nervous men don't pay in advance. Somebody wanted you kept here, asleep, and watched. I don't know why yet. I intend to find out.",choices:[{text:"Then we want the same thing.",next:null,set:{wrenAlly:!0}}]},insightFail:{speaker:"Wren Ashby",text:"I know you snore. That's all I'll admit to for free.",choices:[{text:"Fair.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Wren Ashby",text:"Still pulling threads. Anything with a spiral on it, bring it to me.",choices:[{text:"Will do.",next:null}]}},tam:{start:{speaker:"Brother Tam",text:"Bless you, traveller. If you're hurt, the temple up the road mends bones and worse. Sister Odile is… direct, but she's good at it.",choices:[{text:"Thanks, Brother.",next:null}]}},tull:{start:{speaker:"Lucky Ferrin Tull",text:"Evening, friend. Ferrin Tull. \"Lucky\", to the crew, though you'll notice the crew are the ones still on the boat and I'm the one on the pier. Pull up a crate. I run an honest game, which means the dice are honest and I am not.",choices:[{text:"Let's play.",action:"gamble"},{text:"What games do you run?",next:"games"},{text:"What's the ship?",next:"ship"},{text:"Not tonight.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Lucky Ferrin Tull",text:"Back for more? The dice missed you. Crown and Anchor if you want it quick, Ship Captain and Crew if you want it fair, Widow's Bones if you want it to hurt. Or a long night of the proper stuff, if your purse can stand it.",choices:[{text:"Let's play.",action:"gamble"},{text:"Remind me of the rules.",next:"games"},{text:"Not tonight.",next:null}]},games:{speaker:"Lucky Ferrin Tull",text:"<b>Crown and Anchor:</b> pick a face, I throw three dice, every match pays you your stake again. Quick and cruel.<br><b>Ship, Captain and Crew:</b> five dice, three throws. Find your six, then your five, then your four, in that order. What's left is cargo; most cargo wins.<br><b>Widow's Bones:</b> three dice each, then roll on if you dare. Closest to twenty-one without going over. Twenty-one exactly pays half again.<br><b>A long night:</b> we play for hours. Read me, bluff me, lean on me. The better you are at that, the more of my purse you take home.",choices:[{text:"Let's play.",action:"gamble"},{text:"Later.",next:null}]},ship:{speaker:"Lucky Ferrin Tull",text:"The Brine Widow. Two masts, shallow draft, a captain who could argue a kraken back down. Been tied up here a month waiting on a cargo that never comes. Hollowmere's got a bad name on the water lately. Ask Vane. Politely.",choices:[{text:"Let's play.",action:"gamble"},{text:"I will.",next:null}]}},vane:{start:{speaker:"Captain Marisol Vane",text:"Boots on my deck that I did not hire. You have the look of someone who goes into holes in the ground for money. Fine. Look around, touch nothing in my cabin, and keep your people off the rigging.",choices:[{text:"Why is a ship this size sitting idle?",next:"idleShip"},{text:"Where do you sail?",next:"ports"},{text:"Could I book passage?",next:"passage"},{text:"Understood, Captain.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Captain Marisol Vane",text:"Still here. So is the Widow. One of us is happier about it than the other.",choices:[{text:"Any word on a cargo?",next:"passage"},{text:"Where do you sail?",next:"ports"},{text:"Carry on, Captain.",next:null}]},idleShip:{speaker:"Captain Marisol Vane",text:"No cargo moves out of Hollowmere. Every merchant on this coast has heard the same story: something under this town is humming, and ships that load here have bad luck. Sailors believe in luck the way priests believe in sin. Until somebody stops the humming, I am a very expensive tavern.",choices:[{text:"Somebody is working on the humming.",next:"working"},{text:"That is a long time to be tied up.",next:null}]},working:{speaker:"Captain Marisol Vane",text:"Then work faster. The day the merchants come back, I sail on the tide, and I will have room aboard for whoever made it happen. Consider that a standing offer.",choices:[{text:"I will hold you to it.",next:null,set:{vanePromise:!0}}]},ports:{speaker:"Captain Marisol Vane",text:"South to Saltmarsh, if the weather holds. East along the reef to the Gilt Coast, where the money is. North, never; the Widow was built for warm water and so was I. Somewhere out there is a port where nobody has heard of Hollowmere. I intend to find it.",choices:[{text:"Sounds like a plan.",next:null}]},passage:{speaker:"Captain Marisol Vane",text:"Not yet. I do not put to sea with an empty hold and a full crew; that is how a captain ends up owing her crew. Finish whatever it is you are doing under this town and ask me again.",choices:[{text:"I will.",next:null}]}},pim:{start:{speaker:"Pim",text:"Are you adventurers? Real ones? I am going to be one. Captain says I have to be able to lift the anchor first. I am working on it.",choices:[{text:"[Persuasion] Tell me something useful about the ship.",check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:10},pass:"useful",fail:"useless"},{text:"Keep at it, Pim.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Pim",text:"Do not play Bones with Tull. Play Crown and Anchor. At least then you know it is the dice robbing you.",choices:[{text:"Noted.",next:null}]},useful:{speaker:"Pim",text:"The old cook, the one before Enna, he hid his tips all over below deck and then died before he told anyone where. Enna found some. She did not find all of them. I am not allowed down there any more.",choices:[{text:"Thanks, Pim.",next:null,set:{pimHint:!0}}]},useless:{speaker:"Pim",text:"The gulls will take food right out of your hand. That is useful. Also there is a rat in the hold called Bishop and you are not to hurt him.",choices:[{text:"Noted.",next:null}]}},enna:{start:{speaker:"Salt-Pot Enna",text:"Galley's mine. You can stand in it. You can even eat in it, if you ask nicely and don't touch the rum barrel, which is for medicinal purposes and the Captain's birthday.",choices:[{text:"A bowl of chowder, please.",action:"chowder",next:null},{text:"Pim says the old cook hid money down here.",next:"cook",req:{flag:"pimHint"}},{text:"Just looking.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Salt-Pot Enna",text:"Chowder's on. It is always on. That is the secret of chowder.",choices:[{text:"A bowl, please.",action:"chowder",next:null},{text:"About the old cook's money…",next:"cook",req:{flag:"pimHint"}},{text:"Carry on.",next:null}]},cook:{speaker:"Salt-Pot Enna",text:"Pim talks too much. Yes, old Marrick squirrelled his coin away like a rat, and yes, I have found some of it. Behind things. Under things. In things I would rather not have put my hand into. If you find any, the bilge is yours; the tip jar is mine.",choices:[{text:"Fair terms.",next:null}]}},carrow:{start:{speaker:"Carrow the Tinker",text:"*hic* I saw 'em. The hood men. One dropped a coin and it ROLLED. Rolled right under the floorboards. Rats got it. Rats get everything. Rats'll have my TOOLS next.",choices:[{text:"Sober up, Carrow.",next:null},{text:"[Persuasion] Tell me more about the coin.",check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:10},pass:"coin",fail:"coinFail"}]},coin:{speaker:"Carrow the Tinker",text:"Gold. Stamped funny. Spiral. Like… like a snail that's watching you. *hic*",choices:[{text:"Noted.",next:null,set:{heardSpiral:!0}}]},coinFail:{speaker:"Carrow the Tinker",text:"*snore*",choices:[{text:"…",next:null}]}},jonquil:{start:{speaker:"Jonquil",text:"♪ Oh the sleeper slept for three long nights, and woke without a coin ♪ — sorry, sorry, it's a work in progress. You're the sleeper, yes? Give me a good story and I'll make you famous.",choices:[{text:"Working on it.",next:null},{text:"[Performance] Let me show you how it's done.",check:{skill:"performance",dc:13},pass:"perf",fail:"perfFail"}]},perf:{speaker:"Jonquil",text:"Oh, you're GOOD. Here, a tip from the crowd. Don't spend it on ale.",action:"giveGold:5",choices:[{text:"Cheers.",next:null}]},perfFail:{speaker:"Jonquil",text:"Well. Stick to the dungeon work.",choices:[{text:"Ouch.",next:null}]}},guard:{start:{speaker:"Guard Hobb",text:"Welcome to Hollowmere. No fighting in the square, no fireballs near the thatch, and if you see anyone with a spiral tattoo, you tell me. Or don't. Honestly they scare me.",choices:[{text:"Understood.",next:null}]}},tilly:{start:{speaker:"Tilly Farrow",text:"Fresh bread! Well, fresh-ish. Hey, you're the one who slept at the Flagon for three days! Grell drew a little moustache on you. It's gone now. Mostly.",choices:[{text:"…Thanks, Tilly.",next:null}]}},roderic:{start:{speaker:"Big Roderic",text:"Used to adventure myself. Then a goblin took my kneecap. Not broke it. TOOK it. Anyway, the guild hall recruits companions if you don't fancy going alone.",choices:[{text:"Good tip.",next:null}]}},sprig:{start:{speaker:"Auntie Sprig",text:"Ooh, an adventurer. Take a biscuit. Take two. You look like you've been under a table for three days.",action:"giveItem:goodberry",choices:[{text:"Thank you, Auntie.",next:null}]}},quill:{start:{speaker:"Master Quill",text:"My shop's just there. Potions, scrolls, and things I bought from adventurers who didn't come back to reclaim them. Very reasonable prices. Very.",choices:[{text:"I'll take a look.",next:null}]}},mabel:{start:{speaker:"Old Mabel",text:"The graveyard sang again last night, dearie. Hymns. Old ones. Backwards. You might mention it to someone with a sword. Oh — you have a sword.",choices:[{text:"I'll look into it.",next:null}]}},fenwick:{start:{speaker:"Fenwick the Cooper",text:"Barrels. I make barrels. Grell buys my barrels. Grell says rats are eating his barrels. That's not barrel quality, that's a rat problem.",choices:[{text:"Agreed.",next:null}]}},locked:{start:{speaker:"Door",text:"The door is locked. Someone inside coughs and pretends not to be home.",choices:[{text:"Leave them be.",next:null}]}},cottager:{start:{speaker:"Sela Ord",text:"You just walked into my house. That is a thing adventurers do, apparently. Mind the rug — it is the only nice thing I own.",choices:[{text:"Sorry. Nice rug.",next:null}]}},cottager2:{start:{speaker:"Rooke",text:"I heard the caves out north went quiet last week. Quiet is worse than loud. Loud you can find.",choices:[{text:"Noted.",next:null}]}},nettle:{start:{speaker:"Old Nettle",text:"Bog witch, they call me. I prefer \"consultant.\" You smell of the Spiral Eye's brew, child. Grey mist. Memory-thief. There's only one who brews it, and he lives under the water to the south.",choices:[{text:"The Sunken Temple?",next:"temple"}]},temple:{speaker:"Old Nettle",text:"Aye. Bring me a vial of the grey mist and I'll tell you how to drink it without losing what's left of you.",choices:[{text:"I have one.",req:{flag:"hasMemoryVial"},next:"vial"},{text:"I'll find one.",next:null}]},vial:{speaker:"Old Nettle",text:"Then here is the trick: you don't drink it. You pour it over the one who brewed it. Memory flows back to where it was stolen from.",choices:[{text:"Understood.",next:null,set:{nettleHint:!0}}]}},priest:{start:{speaker:"Sister Odile",text:"Welcome to the temple. Healing is free for those who can't pay and cheap for those who can. Curses cost extra. What do you need?",choices:[]}},ysolde:{start:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"Shut the door, the wind gets in. Sit. You came UP the stair? On purpose? …Well. I'm Ysolde. This is the Cold Comfort, last warm room on the Widow's Tooth. I've written to the guild in Hollowmere eleven times this year about what's on this mountain. You're the first answer.",choices:[{text:"What IS on this mountain?",next:"mountain"},{text:'Why "the Widow\'s Tooth"?',next:"widow"},{text:"I'll hear it later. What have you got for sale?",next:null,action:"shop:waystation"}]},mountain:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"A dragon. Red. Old. She sits on the crown and breathes out a grey fog that rolls down the valley and takes your yesterdays with it. Everyone who goes up comes down not knowing why they went. The hobgoblins on the stair work for her, the fire-cult in the chapel prays to her, and the dead knight in the hold has been waiting two hundred years to kill her. It's a busy mountain.",choices:[{text:"The grey fog. Memory-thief. I've met it.",next:"mist"},{text:"Then let's start with the stair.",next:null}]},mist:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"Then you know. The Spiral Eye down in the valley learned to bottle it, but they didn't make it. She did. Bring her down and the fog stops. Bring her down and maybe some of us get our yesterdays back.",choices:[{text:"Where do I start?",next:null}]},widow:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"Every keeper of this waystation has been a widow. The mountain makes them. Mine was Aldous. He went up with a lantern and a bad idea and came back down with nothing in his head but her name and a smile I didn't know. He walked back up the next morning. I keep the fire lit in case he comes down again.",choices:[{text:"I'm sorry.",next:"sorry"},{text:"I'll bring him down, or bring down the thing that took him.",next:"sorry"}]},sorry:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"Don't be sorry. Be careful, and come back down remembering my name. That's all I ask of anyone.",choices:[{text:"Ysolde. I'll remember.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"The kettle's on. The hearth's yours. The rockfalls on the trail shift when the things holding them are dealt with, so clear a site on each tier and the way up opens. What do you need?",choices:[{text:"Buy supplies.",next:null,action:"shop:waystation"},{text:"Sleep by the hearth (long rest).",next:null,action:"longRest"},{text:"Tell me about the mountain again.",next:"mountain"},{text:"Just warming up.",next:null}]}},dorran:{start:{speaker:"Dorran Kettle",text:"You. The one who got me off that pump. Dorran Kettle, smith, formerly of the Kettle Mine, currently of Ysolde's hearth. I owe you a blade. Trouble is, I've nothing worth forging up here… unless you find me dragon-iron. The old knights of Frostfang had a sword of it. The Frostbrand. If a shard of that came my way, I could make you something she'd remember.",choices:[{text:"[Give the Frostbrand shard] Reforge it.",reqItem:"frostbrandShard",action:"reforge",next:"forged"},{text:"I'll keep an eye out.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"Dorran Kettle",text:"Hammer's warm. Got anything worth hitting?",choices:[{text:"[Give the Frostbrand shard] Reforge it.",reqItem:"frostbrandShard",action:"reforge",next:"forged"},{text:"Not yet.",next:null}]},forged:{speaker:"Dorran Kettle",text:"Three days, a bucket of Frostfang snow, and every swear word I know. There. Wyrmbane. It's cold enough to hurt a red wyrm through her own fire, and it'll know her when it sees her. Don't sell it. Don't drop it. Don't die with it.",choices:[{text:"Thank you, Dorran.",next:null}]},done:{speaker:"Dorran Kettle",text:"How's the blade treating you? Good. Don't answer, just go stick it in something.",choices:[{text:"On my way.",next:null}]}},hermit:{start:{speaker:"The Hermit of the Cairns",text:"Sit, sit. I've nothing to steal and nothing to forget; I traded all that away years ago. The Cairns behind me were the Ash Court's once, the dragon-speakers. Their crown is still down there, somewhere, in the keeping of something that doesn't want visitors. If you bring me the lens they used to look through the mist, the Ash-Glass, I'll show you where the crown is kept.",choices:[{text:"[Give the Ash-Glass Lens] I found it.",reqItem:"ashGlass",action:"tradeAshGlass",next:"crown"},{text:"What else is worth finding up here?",next:"relics"},{text:"Later, hermit.",next:null}]},relics:{speaker:"The Hermit of the Cairns",text:"Three things on this mountain hurt her. A blade the frost-knights made and broke. A disc of her own cooled fire that the chapel wears and thinks is holy. And the crown, which she gave to the Court in a better century, and which her get still obey. Find one and you'll survive her. Find all three and she'll be the one afraid.",choices:[{text:"Where is the crown?",next:"start"}]},crown:{speaker:"The Hermit of the Cairns",text:"The Ash-Glass. Look. Look through it… see? The mist has faces in it. One of them is yours, younger. Now: the crown.",choices:[{text:"Take the Cinder Crown.",next:"given"}]},given:{speaker:"The Hermit of the Cairns",text:"Under the third cairn, where I buried it when I stopped wanting to be anyone. Wear it and her kin will kneel. Wear it and, perhaps, remember to be kind to what kneels.",choices:[{text:"I will.",next:null}]},idle:{speaker:"The Hermit of the Cairns",text:"Still here. Still nothing to steal. The mist's thinner today; did you do that?",choices:[{text:"[Give the Ash-Glass Lens] I found it.",reqItem:"ashGlass",action:"tradeAshGlass",next:"crown"},{text:"Remind me: what hurts her?",next:"relics"},{text:"Keep warm, hermit.",next:null}]}}},acts:[{id:"act1",act:1,title:"Something in the Cellar",giver:"Bosun Grell",dungeon:"cellar",theme:"cellar",level:1,rooms:5,objective:{type:"boss",item:"sigilCoin"},summary:"Clear the rats from the Rusty Flagon's cellar and find whatever they've been hoarding.",twist:"The rats have a king. And the king has your purse: empty except for one gold coin stamped with a spiral of eyes.",bossIntro:"Atop a throne of stolen cheese and broken casks sits a rat the size of a dog, wearing a bottlecap for a crown. Something glints in its nest: a coin purse. Yours.",complete:{speaker:"Bosun Grell",text:"A rat KING? In MY cellar? …Well. That explains the tiny crown I found in the drain. That coin, though: same as the one the hooded man paid with. Take it to the temple, Sister Odile collects odd coins. Keep the room; you've earned it.",reward:{gold:25,xp:300,item:"potionHealing"}},unlocks:"act2"},{id:"act2",act:2,title:"The Spiral Coin",giver:"Sister Odile",dungeon:"caves",theme:"cave",level:2,rooms:7,objective:{type:"boss",item:"cultLetter"},summary:"Sister Odile recognizes the sigil: the Spiral Eye, a cult that trades with the goblins of Gnawtooth Caverns. Find out what the goblins know.",twist:'The goblin boss, cornered, offers a deal: he sold "the sleeper" to hooded men for two hundred gold. He has their letter. The sleeper was you.',bossIntro:"The goblin boss rises from a throne of stolen saddles, crown askew. \"Wait, wait, WAIT. I know you. You're the sleeper! They said you wouldn't wake up for a YEAR!\"",bossChoice:{text:'The Goblin Boss drops his scimitars and holds up a folded letter. "Two hundred gold they gave me for you. Take the letter. Take the gold. Just don\'t take my crown."',options:[{text:'[Persuasion DC 12] "Tell me everything and walk away."',check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:12},pass:"The boss babbles: hooded men, a temple under the swamp, a brewer named Voskar. He flees with his crown. The letter and gold are yours.",fail:'He squints. "You\'re bluffing." The goblins attack!',spare:!0},{text:'[Intimidation DC 10] "The crown too."',check:{skill:"intimidation",dc:10},pass:"He throws the crown, the letter, and the gold, and runs squealing into the dark. You now own a goblin crown.",fail:'He shrieks "NEVER!" and the goblins attack!',spare:!0,extraGold:20},{text:"No deals. Attack!",fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Sister Odile",text:"A letter. \"The forgetful one wakes at the Flagon. Watch them.\" Written in the cult's hand. They didn't kidnap you at random, {name}: they're afraid of what you know. Old Mabel says the graveyard's been singing. The Spiral Eye raises the dead when it wants a congregation. Go and see.",reward:{gold:60,xp:600,item:"scroll_bless"}},unlocks:"act3"},{id:"act3",act:3,title:"Whispers in the Crypt",giver:"Sister Odile",dungeon:"crypt",theme:"crypt",level:3,rooms:8,objective:{type:"boss",item:"memoryVial"},summary:"Cultists of the Spiral Eye are raising the dead in the Ashwood Crypt. Stop the ritual and learn why they fear you.",twist:'The cult fanatic leading the ritual knows your face. "You came to STOP us. You nearly did. Voskar took your memories instead of your life. He\'s sentimental like that."',bossIntro:'Candles guttering, a fanatic in violet stands over an open sarcophagus. She turns. Her eyes widen. "The investigator. You\'re supposed to be asleep. Voskar said the brew would hold for a YEAR."',complete:{speaker:"Sister Odile",text:"So you were hunting them before they caught you. That's… actually comforting. This vial: grey mist, the brew that took your memory. There's a bog witch in Brackenmoor, west road, who knows that kind of alchemy. And Wren says the bandits at Redwatch Fort were paid to deliver \"a sleeper.\" Follow the money.",reward:{gold:100,xp:900,item:"ringProtection"},unlockTown:"brackenmoor"},unlocks:"act4"},{id:"act4",act:4,title:"The Toll Road",giver:"Wren Ashby",dungeon:"fort",theme:"fort",level:4,rooms:8,objective:{type:"boss",item:"captainLedger",rescue:!0},summary:"The Redwatch bandits were paid to carry you to the Flagon. Take their fort, take their ledger, and free whoever else they're holding.",twist:"The Bandit Captain is done with the cult: they paid in cursed coin and half her crew won't sleep. She'll trade the ledger for her life. And a prisoner in the cells is an adventurer who was hunting the cult with you.",bossIntro:'The Bandit Captain leans on a table piled with spiral-stamped coins. "Let me guess. The sleeper. You know those bastards paid us with coins that whisper? Half my lads haven\'t slept in a week."',bossChoice:{text:'"Here\'s my offer. The ledger, the prisoner, and the cursed coin. You walk out, we ride out, and nobody bleeds."',options:[{text:"[Insight DC 13] Is she telling the truth?",check:{skill:"insight",dc:13},pass:"She is. Terrified, in fact. She hands over the ledger and the keys, and the bandits file out into the hills. The cursed coins you leave behind.",fail:"You can't read her. She takes your hesitation as refusal and draws steel!",spare:!0},{text:"Take the deal.",spare:!0,pass:"She tosses you the ledger and the keys and is gone within the minute. Smart woman."},{text:"Bandits don't get deals. Attack!",fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Wren Ashby",text:'The ledger: "Delivered the sleeper. 200gp. — V." Voskar. Voice of the Spiral Eye. He\'s in the Sunken Temple south of Brackenmoor, and the bog witch says the mist can be turned back on him. This is it, {name}. Finish it.',reward:{gold:150,xp:1200,item:"potionGreaterHealing",companion:!0}},unlocks:"act5"},{id:"act5",act:5,title:"The Sunken Temple",giver:"Wren Ashby",dungeon:"temple",theme:"temple",level:5,rooms:9,objective:{type:"boss"},summary:"Descend into the Sunken Temple and confront Voskar, Voice of the Spiral Eye, the man who stole your memories.",twist:"Voskar offers your memories back, freely, if you kneel. He remembers the person you were. He liked them better.",bossIntro:"Water drips into a black pool. Voskar turns, smiling like an old friend. \"{name}! You found your way back. You always were stubborn. Kneel, and I'll give you back every day I took. You'll remember why you came the first time. You'll remember that you almost said yes.\"",bossChoice:{text:"The Voice of the Spiral Eye holds out a vial of grey mist. Your mist.",options:[{text:"[Wisdom save DC 15] Resist his voice and attack.",save:"wis",dc:15,pass:'His words slide off you like rain. "Pity," he sighs, and the temple erupts.',fail:"For a moment you almost kneel. He laughs. That laugh is the only thing that saves you: nobody kneels to a laugh like that. Roll initiative, at disadvantage.",fight:!0},{text:"Throw the memory vial at him (bog witch's trick).",req:"nettleHint",pass:"The mist bursts across his face. He screams. Memories, yours and his, pour back into you like cold water. He staggers, weakened. Now: finish it.",fight:!0,weakenBoss:!0},{text:"\"I don't need to remember to know I'd say no.\" Attack!",fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Wren Ashby",text:"It's over. Voskar's gone, the cult's scattered, and Hollowmere can sleep. Including you, if you like. Under a table, even. As for your memories… the mist is broken. What comes back will come back. And if it doesn't? You made a pretty good life in a week. Make another.<br><br>One more thing. Voskar didn't invent that mist. His notes say he learned it from \"the Widow on the Tooth.\" There's a road north of the square that climbs into the cloud. A waystation keeper up there, Ysolde Hask, has been writing to the guild for a year. Nobody answered. Maybe you should.",reward:{gold:300,xp:2e3,item:"diceOfFate"}},unlocks:"act6"},{id:"act6",act:6,title:"The Goatherds' Stair",giver:"Ysolde Hask",dungeon:"kettle",theme:"mine",level:6,rooms:7,objective:{type:"boss"},bossId:"hobgoblinCaptain",bossMinions:"hobgoblin",summary:"Hobgoblins hold the Kettle Mine and the smith who worked it, Dorran Kettle. Clear them out and bring him down the stair alive.",twist:"The captain is not holding the mine for copper. Something above told her to hold the stair, and she is far more afraid of it than of you.",bossIntro:'A hobgoblin in red lacquer sits on an upturned ore cart, a greatsword across her knees. Behind her, chained to the pump, a soot-black dwarf raises an eyebrow at you. "Took your time." The captain stands. "Nobody goes up. Those are the orders. I don\'t like them either."',bossChoice:{text:'"Orders from whom?" you ask. She glances up, at the roof of the mine, at the mountain above it.',options:[{text:'[Intimidation DC 14] "Tell me what\'s up there, and take your warband down the mountain."',check:{skill:"intimidation",dc:14},pass:"She weighs you, then the ceiling. \"A wyrm. Red. She breathes a grey fog that takes your yesterdays. My scouts came back not knowing their own names.\" She tosses you the dwarf's keys. \"Stair's yours. Don't say I didn't warn you.\"",fail:'She laughs without humour. "I\'ve been threatened by worse. Much worse. Recently." Steel.',spare:!0,extraGold:60},{text:'[Persuasion DC 13] "Whatever it is, I\'m going up anyway. Let the smith go."',check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:13},pass:'"Mad," she says, almost kindly, and unlocks the dwarf herself. "Then take him. You\'ll want a smith where you\'re going." Her warband files out past you, eyes down.',fail:'"Sentiment. Wonderful. Kill them."',spare:!0},{text:"No deals with slavers. Attack!",fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"Dorran Kettle, alive, and complaining about the stair. That's the first good news up here in a year. He'll set up at my hearth; he says he owes you a blade, and Dorran keeps his debts. {name}: the captain's \"orders\" came from the crown of the mountain. My husband went up there. He didn't come back down remembering me. Frostfang Hold is next on the trail. Something there kept the old oath against the wyrm.",reward:{gold:200,xp:2500},setFlags:{dorranFreed:!0}},unlocks:"act7"},{id:"act7",act:7,title:"The Oath of Frostfang",giver:"Ysolde Hask",dungeon:"frostfang",theme:"fort",level:7,rooms:8,objective:{type:"boss",item:"frostbrandShard",keep:!0},bossId:"frostWight",bossMinions:"skeleton",summary:"Frostfang Hold was built to watch the dragon. Its last knight still holds it, two hundred years dead. Learn what he knows and bring back the Frostbrand, the blade that was forged to end her.",twist:"Sir Halden Frost swore to stand until the wyrm was dead. He remembers every day of the two centuries since. He is the only creature on the mountain the mist could never touch, because he has nothing left to forget.",bossIntro:'Frost on the banners, frost on the throne, frost on the knight who rises from it with a sound like ice breaking. Blue light in an iron helm. "Two hundred and eleven years. Do you know how many came up this stair in that time? Eleven. You are the twelfth." He lifts a broken sword. "State your oath."',bossChoice:{text:"The shard of the Frostbrand glows in his fist. He waits, as he has always waited.",options:[{text:"[Religion DC 14] Kneel and swear the old oath: to stand against the wyrm until she is dead or you are.",check:{skill:"religion",dc:14},pass:'The words come out of you in a language you did not know you knew. The knight goes very still. Then he kneels, and lays the shard at your feet. "Then my watch is ended." Blue light gutters out of the helm. The hold is quiet.',fail:'You stumble on the third line. "No," he says. "Not an oath-keeper. A tourist." He swings.',spare:!0},{text:'[Persuasion DC 15] "You\'ve kept your oath. Let someone else carry the blade."',check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:15},pass:'"…Carry it, then." He drops the shard. He does not sit back down; he simply stops, like a clock.',fail:'"Sweet words. She spoke sweetly too." The dead knight attacks.',spare:!0},{text:"Take the blade from his cold hands. Attack!",fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"The Frostbrand. Even broken it makes the hearth burn blue. Take it to Dorran. He's the last smith alive who has worked dragon-iron, and he's been itching for something worth hammering. While he works: the Cinder Chapel across the shoulder. Fire-cult. They pray to her. They have something she wants back.",reward:{gold:250,xp:3e3}},unlocks:"act8"},{id:"act8",act:8,title:"The Cinder Chapel",giver:"Ysolde Hask",dungeon:"chapel",theme:"temple",level:8,rooms:8,objective:{type:"boss",item:"emberWard",keep:!0},bossId:"emberPriest",bossMinions:"emberZealot",summary:"The Cinder Chapel burns memories as offerings to the dragon. Its priest keeps the Ember Ward, a disc of cooled dragonglass that drinks fire. Stop the ritual and take it.",twist:"The chapel does not steal memories. People bring their own, and pay to have them burned. The priest thinks he is offering mercy. Some of Hollowmere's missing are on his benches.",bossIntro:"Heat. A brazier the size of a cart, and around it a congregation with empty, peaceful faces. The priest turns, robes smouldering at the hem, a black glass disc on his chest. \"Another pilgrim! What would you like to forget? Everyone has something. Sit. Sit. It doesn't hurt. That's rather the point.\"",bossChoice:{text:"The Ember Ward pulses on his chest with the rhythm of the brazier. The congregation does not look up.",options:[{text:"[Arcana DC 15] Unpick the ritual: the ward is the anchor. Break the link.",check:{skill:"arcana",dc:15},pass:'You see it: every burned memory feeds the disc, and the disc feeds the fire. You speak the word that cuts the thread. The brazier roars, then guts. The priest staggers, half his power gone with it. "What have you DONE—"',fail:"You reach for the thread and the fire reaches back. It hurts. It was, in fact, the point.",fight:!0,weakenBoss:!0},{text:'[Persuasion DC 15] "Give me the ward and walk away with them. She won\'t thank you for this."',check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:15},pass:'He looks at the disc for a long moment. "…She never has, has she." He unclasps it and presses it into your hands, warm as a heartbeat, and leads his flock out into the snow.',fail:'"Walk away? From MERCY?" The congregation rises as one.',spare:!0},{text:"Kick over the brazier. Attack!",fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"The Ember Ward. Wear it up there and her fire will only warm you. The people you brought down don't remember why they went up. That's… kinder than the alternative, I think. One more door before the crown: the Wyrm's Gullet, where the mountain breathes out. Whatever is in there is hers.",reward:{gold:300,xp:3500}},unlocks:"act9"},{id:"act9",act:9,title:"The Wyrm's Gullet",giver:"Ysolde Hask",dungeon:"gullet",theme:"cave",level:9,rooms:8,objective:{type:"boss"},bossId:"redWyrmling",bossMinions:"magmaMephit",summary:"The Gullet is the mountain's throat, the last cave before the crown. Something young and hot guards it. Clear the way to the summit.",twist:"The wyrmling is her child. It remembers you. You were here before, on the day you lost your memory, and you turned back at this exact spot.",bossIntro:'The cave opens onto a ledge over a river of slow red light. On the ledge, a dragon the size of a horse uncoils, and its eyes go wide. "YOU. You came back! Mother said you wouldn\'t. Mother said the mist would hold." It grins with far too many teeth. "She was so ANGRY when you got away."',bossChoice:{text:"The wyrmling paces the ledge, delighted and deadly, waiting to see what you do this time.",options:[{text:'[Cinder Crown] "Kneel, hatchling. The Ash Court commands it."',reqItem:"cinderCrown",pass:'The crown burns cold on your brow and the words are not quite yours. The wyrmling flattens itself to the stone, wings over its head, and whimpers. "Yes. Yes, my lord. The way is open. Don\'t tell her I—" It flees down the river of light.',spare:!0,extraGold:100},{text:"[Insight DC 14] Read the beast. What does it actually want?",check:{skill:"insight",dc:14},pass:"It wants her to notice it. Every word is a performance for a mother who is not watching. You say so. It shrieks, and the fight is on, but it fights like a child throwing a tantrum: badly.",fail:"You misread it. It was not talking to you. It was stalling. Its breath is already glowing.",fight:!0,weakenBoss:!0},{text:'"Tell your mother I\'m coming." Attack!',fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"Then the crown is open, and it's time. {name}, listen. I don't know what you'll find up there. My Aldous came back down with nothing in his head but her name and a smile I didn't recognise. He walked back up the next morning. Bring her down, or bring something better than a blade. Either way: come back down remembering. Promise me that.",reward:{gold:400,xp:4500},setFlags:{summitOpen:!0}},unlocks:"act10"},{id:"act10",act:10,title:"The Widow's Tooth",giver:"Ysolde Hask",dungeon:"summit",theme:"lair",level:12,rooms:9,objective:{type:"boss"},bossId:"ashkaraz",bossMinions:"magmaMephit",summary:"Climb into the crown of the Widow's Tooth and face Ashkaraz, the red dragon whose cooled breath is the memory-mist. End it, one way or another.",twist:"Ashkaraz brewed the mist for herself. She had something she could not bear to remember, and she has breathed it out over the valley for a hundred years rather than face it. She no longer knows what it was. The cult, Voskar, your three lost days: all of it, the runoff of one creature's grief.",bossIntro:'The summit is a bowl of black glass and half-melted gold, open to a sky the colour of a bruise. She is coiled at its centre, red as a wound, and she does not get up. "The one who got away." Her voice is the mountain talking. "I forgot your face. I forget everyone\'s face. It is the only mercy I have left, and you have come to take it from me." Smoke curls from her nostrils. "Well. Come, then."',bossChoice:{text:"Ashkaraz rises. Coins slide off her flanks like water. Behind her, the hoard of a hundred years; in front of her, you.",options:[{text:"[Wyrmbane] Draw the Frostbrand reforged and let her see it.",reqItem:"wyrmbane",pass:"She sees the blade and, for one heartbeat, she remembers something: two hundred years ago, a knight, this steel, a wound that never quite healed. She flinches. It is all the opening you will ever get.",fight:!0,surpriseBoss:!0},{text:'[Cinder Crown] "By the Ash Court, your servants are dismissed. This is between us."',reqItem:"cinderCrown",pass:'The mephits and hounds of her court hear the crown speak and scatter shrieking into the cracks. Ashkaraz watches them go with something like contempt, and something like fear. "That crown was mine once," she says. "I gave it away. I do not remember why."',fight:!0,noMinions:!0,loseLegendary:!0},{text:"[Ember Ward] Walk into her first breath and let the ward drink it.",reqItem:"emberWard",pass:"She breathes. The world goes white and orange and the ward on your chest goes hot as a coal and DRINKS. You are standing in the middle of a firestorm, singed and alive. She has spent her breath before the fight has begun, and she knows it.",fight:!0,spendBreath:!0},{text:"[Persuasion DC 18] \"You don't remember why you're angry. Neither do I. Let it go.\"",check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:18},pass:'A long silence. Ash falls. "…No," she says at last, quietly. "I don\'t." She looks at her hoard as if seeing it for the first time. "Take what you want. I am going somewhere cold, to remember, or to stop." The greatest wyrm of the age lifts into the bruised sky and does not look back. The mist over the valley begins, at last, to thin.',fail:'"Let it GO?" The word is a wall of fire. Roll initiative.',spare:!0,extraGold:500},{text:'"For Hollowmere, and for three days I\'ll never get back." Attack!',fight:!0}]},complete:{speaker:"Ysolde Hask",text:"You came down. You came down remembering. Sit. Sit by the fire, all of you.<br><br>The mist over the valley is gone. I woke this morning and remembered my Aldous's laugh, the real one, and I have been crying into the kettle ever since, and I am not sorry. Hollowmere will remember too. Every purse-thief and hooded fool who ever bought a vial of grey fog is out of business tonight.<br><br>The Tooth is yours now. Her hoard is still up there, and things will move into it; things always do. Go and get rich. You've earned it, {name}. Twice.",reward:{gold:1e3,xp:8e3,item:"amuletHealth"}},unlocks:"endless"}],randomQuests:[{id:"missing",title:"Missing Villagers",text:"Three villagers went to {dungeon} on a dare and never came back. Find them.",objective:"rescue",twists:['The villagers were not kidnapped. They joined. One of them tries to convince you the monsters are "misunderstood."',"Only one villager remains. The other two were eaten. She is very calm about it.","The villagers are alive but the monsters are holding them for ransom. The ransom is a pie."]},{id:"hunt",title:"Monster Hunt",text:"Something in {dungeon} has been taking livestock. The farmers will pay for its head.",objective:"boss",twists:["The beast is guarding a litter of young. Killing it is easy. Deciding to is not.",'The "beast" is a very large, very hungry man in a bear pelt. He surrenders immediately.',"The monster was already dead when you arrived. Something bigger killed it. Something still here."]},{id:"artifact",title:"The Cursed Artifact",text:"A relic in {dungeon} has been making the locals dream of teeth. Bring it back for the temple to cleanse.",objective:"item",item:"templeIdol",twists:["The relic is not cursed. The temple acolyte who posted the quest is. He wanted it for himself.","The relic whispers offers of power as you carry it. It is quite persuasive.","The relic is a very ordinary idol. The dreams were caused by the cheese from the same farm."]},{id:"caravan",title:"The Lost Caravan",text:"A merchant caravan vanished near {dungeon}. Recover the manifest and any cargo that survived.",objective:"item",item:"caravanManifest",twists:["The caravan was carrying cult reagents. The merchant knew exactly who he was selling to.","The caravan's guards took the cargo and staged the attack themselves.","The cargo was a single, very angry mimic. It has eaten two bandits and is grateful for the company."]},{id:"ruins",title:"Ancient Ruins",text:"A scholar wants the runes in {dungeon} transcribed. Bring back the tablet.",objective:"item",item:"ancientTablet",twists:["The runes are a recipe. A very good one, for bread.","The tablet is a warning: DO NOT REMOVE THE TABLET. You have removed the tablet.","The scholar is a lich in disguise. Well, was. He's retired. He just really likes runes."]},{id:"locket",title:"The Lost Locket",text:"An old woman lost a silver locket in {dungeon} fifty years ago. She would like it back before she dies. She is very specific about that.",objective:"item",item:"lostLocket",twists:["The locket holds a portrait of the monster now living in the dungeon. It was her husband.","The old woman is the monster's mother. She wanted the locket to remember him by.","The locket contains a map to a second, much better treasure. She knew."]},{id:"escort",title:"Escort the Pilgrim",text:"A pilgrim needs safe passage to a shrine deep in {dungeon}. Keep them alive.",objective:"boss",escort:!0,twists:["The pilgrim is the boss's long-lost sibling. The reunion is awkward but bloodless.","The pilgrim is a cult spy. He tries to slip away at the shrine.","The pilgrim is extremely competent and mostly wants company. Also snacks."]},{id:"investigation",title:"Strange Lights",text:"Lights and chanting in {dungeon} at midnight. Investigate.",objective:"clue",twists:["It's a birthday party for a goblin. You were, technically, not invited.","It's a cult ritual. The cult is very small. It is two people and a goat.","The lights are a trapped will-o'-wisp begging to be freed. Freeing it is a terrible idea. You will do it anyway."]}],events:[{id:"woundedGoblin",text:'A goblin lies against the wall, clutching a wounded leg. It looks up at you with enormous, wet eyes. "Please. No stab. Have gold. Have SECRET."',choices:[{text:"[Medicine DC 10] Bandage its leg.",check:{skill:"medicine",dc:10},pass:{text:'It blinks, stunned. "Big-folk is… nice?" It tells you where a hidden cache is and limps away. The spot is marked on your map.',revealSecret:!0,xp:50},fail:{text:"You make it worse. It screams, hobbles off, and the whole dungeon probably heard.",alert:!0}},{text:'[Intimidation DC 10] "The secret. Now."',check:{skill:"intimidation",dc:10},pass:{text:'"Chest in the back room is TRAP. Real gold under the loose stone!" It hands you a pouch and flees.',gold:15,xp:50},fail:{text:"It sneers, throws a rock at you (1 damage), and vanishes down a crack in the wall.",damage:1}},{text:"Take its gold and leave it.",pass:{text:"You take the pouch. It mutters something rude in Goblin.",gold:8}}]},{id:"ghostMerchant",text:'A translucent merchant floats beside a ghostly cart. "Wares! Fine wares! Slightly dead wares!" He wants payment in gold. He is very insistent that ghosts still need gold.',choices:[{text:"Buy a mystery potion. (20 gp)",cost:20,pass:{text:'He hands you a glowing bottle and fades, whispering "no refunds."',item:"random:potion"}},{text:"[Persuasion DC 13] Haggle.",check:{skill:"persuasion",dc:13},pass:{text:'"For YOU? Free. Take it and stop making eye contact."',item:"random:potion",xp:50},fail:{text:'"Cheapskate!" He vanishes, cart and all.'}},{text:"Walk away from the dead salesman.",pass:{text:"He shouts prices after you until you turn the corner."}}]},{id:"cursedIdol",text:'An idol of the Spiral Eye sits on a plinth. Its eyes track you. A voice like wet velvet whispers: "Take me. I know what you\'ve forgotten."',choices:[{text:"[Wisdom save DC 12] Resist and smash it.",save:"wis",dc:12,pass:{text:"You bring your weapon down. It shatters with a scream and leaves behind a handful of gemstones.",gold:30,xp:75},fail:{text:"Your hand freezes. You hear a name you almost recognise. When you come to, the idol is gone and you feel weaker.",status:"weakened"}},{text:"[Arcana DC 12] Study the enchantment first.",check:{skill:"arcana",dc:12},pass:{text:"A memory-trap keyed to the mist. You disarm it with a word and pocket the gems.",gold:30,xp:100},fail:{text:"Poking it was a mistake. Psychic backlash: 1d6 damage.",damageRoll:"1d6"}},{text:"Leave it alone.",pass:{text:"Wise. The whispering follows you out of the room."}}]},{id:"trappedAdventurer",text:'A dwarf hangs upside down in a snare, arms crossed, dignified. "Don\'t. Say. Anything."',choices:[{text:"[Athletics DC 10] Cut her down carefully.",check:{skill:"athletics",dc:10},pass:{text:'She lands on her feet, dusts herself off, and hands you a potion. "We never speak of this."',item:"potionHealing",xp:50},fail:{text:'She lands on her head. "…Thanks." She limps off with what dignity remains.',xp:25}},{text:"Say something.",pass:{text:'"Hanging around?" She frees herself with a knife out of pure spite and leaves.'}}]},{id:"shrine",text:"A small shrine to a forgotten god. A bowl for offerings sits before it, holding two copper pieces and a button.",choices:[{text:"Offer 10 gold.",cost:10,pass:{text:"Warmth floods through you. The party is blessed.",partyStatus:"bless"}},{text:"[Religion DC 11] Say the proper rite.",check:{skill:"religion",dc:11},pass:{text:"The old words come easily. Everyone feels restored.",healParty:"2d8",xp:50},fail:{text:"You mispronounce the god's name. The button vanishes. Nothing else happens. Probably."}},{text:"Take the copper.",pass:{text:"You take two copper and a button. You feel a little worse about yourself.",gold:1}}]},{id:"prisoner",text:'A figure sits in a locked cage: an adventurer, bruised but alive. "About time. Get me out and I owe you a favour."',rescue:!0,choices:[{text:"[Sleight of Hand DC 12] Pick the lock.",check:{skill:"sleightOfHand",dc:12,tools:!0},pass:{text:"Click. The cage swings open.",companion:!0,xp:75},fail:{text:'The pick snaps. "Try the other way."',retry:!0}},{text:"[Athletics DC 14] Bend the bars.",check:{skill:"athletics",dc:14},pass:{text:'The bars groan and give. "…Remind me not to arm-wrestle you."',companion:!0,xp:75},fail:{text:"The bars win. The prisoner sighs politely.",retry:!0}},{text:"Look for a key elsewhere.",pass:{text:"You leave them for now. The key must be somewhere in this dungeon.",retry:!0}}]},{id:"library",text:"Shelves of mouldering books. One is chained shut and hums faintly.",choices:[{text:"[Investigation DC 12] Search the shelves.",check:{skill:"investigation",dc:12},pass:{text:"Behind a false book: a scroll case.",item:"random:scroll",xp:50},fail:{text:"You find a recipe for goblin stew and a lot of dust."}},{text:"[Arcana DC 14] Open the chained book.",check:{skill:"arcana",dc:14},pass:{text:"Knowledge floods your mind. You feel wiser and slightly ill.",xp:150},fail:{text:"The book bites you. 1d4 damage. Books should not bite.",damageRoll:"1d4"}},{text:"Leave the books.",pass:{text:"The humming follows you out."}}]},{id:"fountain",text:"A fountain of dark water. Coins glitter at the bottom. The water is perfectly still.",choices:[{text:"Drink.",save:"con",dc:11,pass:{text:"Cold and clean. You feel refreshed.",healParty:"1d8"},fail:{text:"It tastes of pennies. You are poisoned.",status:"poisoned"}},{text:"[Sleight of Hand DC 10] Fish out the coins.",check:{skill:"sleightOfHand",dc:10},pass:{text:"Quick fingers, dry sleeves.",gold:12},fail:{text:"Something in the water grabs your wrist. You yank free, minus a coin or two, plus a scratch.",damage:2}},{text:"Leave it.",pass:{text:"Still water. Best left still."}}]},{id:"gambler",text:"A skeleton sits at a table with a cup of dice. It rattles the cup at you invitingly.",choices:[{text:"Roll against it. (10 gp)",cost:10,contest:!0,pass:{text:"You roll higher! The skeleton slumps, defeated, and slides over its winnings.",gold:30,xp:50},fail:{text:"It rolls a 20. Of course it does. It rattles smugly."}},{text:"Smash the skeleton.",pass:{text:"It doesn't fight back. Under its ribs: a few coins.",gold:6}},{text:"Decline politely.",pass:{text:"It shrugs. Bones clatter."}}]}],riddles:[{q:"I have keys but open no locks. I have space but no room. You can enter but not go inside. What am I?",a:["keyboard","a keyboard"],options:["A keyboard","A dungeon","A coffin","A map"],correct:0},{q:"The more you take, the more you leave behind. What am I?",options:["Gold","Footsteps","Time","Breath"],correct:1},{q:"I am not alive, but I grow. I have no lungs, but I need air. I have no mouth, but water kills me.",options:["A tree","A shadow","Fire","Rust"],correct:2},{q:"What has one eye but cannot see?",options:["A cyclops","A needle","A storm","A wizard"],correct:1},{q:"Feed me and I live. Give me a drink and I die.",options:["A goblin","A fire","A sword","A rat"],correct:1},{q:"I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body but come alive with wind.",options:["A ghost","A bell","An echo","A flute"],correct:2},{q:"What can run but never walks, has a mouth but never talks, has a bed but never sleeps?",options:["A river","A dog","A sleeper","A road"],correct:0}],leverHints:['"First the sun, then the moon, then the stars, then the dark." (The levers are marked with those signs.)','"Left is right when the eye is closed." (The order is reversed: right to left.)','"Pull the odd ones first."'],dungeonFlavor:{cellar:["The smell of sour ale and wet fur.","Something scurries behind the casks.","Cheese. Someone has been hoarding cheese."],cave:["Water drips somewhere ahead.","Goblin graffiti covers the wall. It is rude.","The tunnel narrows. Torchlight flickers on damp stone."],crypt:["The air is cold and tastes of dust.","Names on the wall niches have been scratched out.","Somewhere, faintly, someone is singing a hymn backwards."],forest:["Roots twist through the ceiling.","Webs. Lots of webs.","Bones of small animals, arranged neatly."],fort:["Banners of a fallen house rot on the walls.","Fresh boot prints. Lots of them.","Someone has been gambling here. Recently."],temple:["Water laps against black stone.","The spiral is carved everywhere. It watches.","Chanting echoes from deeper in."],mine:["Timbers creak overhead.","A pickaxe lies abandoned mid-swing.","Copper glints in the walls."],swamp:["Everything is damp.","The green light flickers between drowned houses.","Frogs. So many frogs."],lair:["The heat hits you like a wall.","Coins. Everywhere, half-melted into the floor.","Scorch marks on the wall in the shape of people.","Somewhere below, something very large breathes in."]}};